From ee74bd74b77c353a1177aeb338455f64fed4cb8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:22:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: generated code compatible with device code

The code generated for the behaviours, the material properties used by
the behaviours and the models can be compiled for GPUs. Host code is
unchanged: device specific code is selected by the TFEL_DEVICE_CODE
macro and returns failures instead of throwing exceptions.

- Host/device annotations of the generated methods (integration,
  prediction and tangent operators, stress free expansion, jacobian and
  tangent operator blocks, isotropic DSLs, Runge-Kutta DSLs, bricks,
  wrappers of behaviour variables, models).
- Helpers writing code which differs on the host and in device code.
- Bounds checks: failure returned in device code (checkBounds returns a
  boolean, physical bounds checked after integration return FAILURE).
- Parameters: an interface may give the values of the parameters to its
  behaviour constructor, since the parameters initializers are host
  singletons. Parameters treated as static variables are constant
  members in device code (static data members can't be odr-used).
- Material properties called by behaviours: the mfront interface also
  writes an implementation in the mfront::device namespace (no exception,
  no errno, NaN if a physical bound is violated), used in device code.
- Interfaces may forbid dynamically allocated vectors.
- Blocks of code written by several interfaces are only written once, so
  that interfaces sharing members (generic and generic-parallel) can be
  used together.
- Profiling disabled in device code.
